      <slug></slug>
      <title>UNO: Anecdotal Evidence</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>OpenOffice.org</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;UNO is the object model underlying OpenOffice.org. With its by now long and winding history, this might be a good time to reflect on its design and implementation, its shortcomings and strengths.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;  </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In this talk we will look at details in various areas of UNO, tell the occasional anecdote, and generally have fun.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;  </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="2181">Stephan Bergmann</person>
      </persons>
